ut T8 is only 1 left. If I discard T6, maybe I can get T8. But that's a long shot.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard W7, maybe I can form a chow with W6 and W7 if I get W8. But again, not sure.\n\nAnother angle: looking at the unshown tiles. For example, W5 is available (4 left). If I can get W5, I can form a chow of W3-W4-W5. So if I discard a tile that allows me to keep W3 and W4, maybe that's better. So if I discard W1, I can keep W3 and W4 for a potential chow with W5. Similarly, if I discard W9, maybe I can keep W7 for a potential chow with W8. But W8 is only 2 left.\n\nSo maybe discarding W1 or W9 would be better. Let's see. If I discard W1, then I have W3, W4, W6, W7, W9. If I draw W5, I can form W3-W4-W5. If I draw W8, I can form W7-W8-W9. That gives me two chows. That would be good. So discarding W1 might be a good idea. But W1 is a terminal tile, which is part of All Terminals if I can form all terminals. But I don't have all terminals.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard W9, similar logic. If I discard W9, then I can get W8 to form W7-W8-W9. So that's another chow.\n\nBut which one is better? Let's check the unshown tiles. W5 has 4 left, W8 has 2 left. So maybe W5 is more available. So discarding W1 allows me to aim for W5, which is more available. So maybe discard W1.\n\nBut W1 is a terminal tile. If I discard it, others might take it for their hands. But if I keep it, I can't form chows with it. So maybe better to discard W1 to get W5.\n\nLooking at the valid actions, Play W1 is an option. So maybe that's a good choice.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard W3 or W4, which are part of a potential chow. For example, if I discard W3, then I can get W2 to form W1-W2-W3. But W2 is available (3 left). However, I have W1, so if I get W2, I can form that chow. But I would need to keep W1. So if I discard W3, I can still keep W1 and W4. If I get W2, that's a chow. But W2 is available. So maybe that's possible.\n\nBut I need to decide which tile to discard. The options are W1,